=== WEB SOURCE → NATIVE PARITY (no scope narrowing, no parity shortcuts) ===
Web `AIYearReviewNarration` = `withAiFeature('yir-narration', InnerSection)` where InnerSection is an
`AIFeatureCard` driven by `useAiStream`. It reads `vehicleId?: number`, computes
`defaultYear = new Date().getFullYear() - 1`, builds a `useMemo` body
`{ vehicle_id: vehicleId ?? 0, year: defaultYear }`, POSTs it to the STATIC url
`/ai/analytics/year-in-review/narrate`, and gates the button on `canStart = vehicleId != null`
(a present id; `0` passes, only nil disables). Card title "Helix narration", a description, the
"Generate narration" verb, the "Helix" badge, feeding `AiOutputPanel`.

Data sources (P1/S8 state-holders, no direct HTTP from the view):
  - useTranslation → YearReviewNarrationStrings facade (NSLocalizedString, per-surface .strings table).
  - useAiStream    → YearReviewNarrationSource seam. The production app implements it over the AI-enabled
                     settings holder + the useAiStream SSE client (which builds the
                     YearReviewNarrationRequest body + drives the connection); previews/tests use
                     InMemoryYearReviewNarrationSource. The pure SSE frame parser + delta-accumulating
                     reducer (verbatim ports of parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent + handleEvent/finalizeError)
                     live in the Adapter and are unit-tested without a network.
Shared components mapped:
  - @/components/ai/AIFeatureCard → reproduced natively as the card chrome + the Ask-Helix button +
    the AiOutputPanel region (header title + Helix badge + description + universal "Ask Helix" button
    whose label flips to "Helix is thinking…" while streaming + the output panel). The web AIFeatureCard
    atom is owned by the P4 component-library bundle (out of scope), so these are private subviews
    scoped to this surface.
  - @/components/ai/withAiFeature → the `.gated` phase collapses the surface to EmptyView (ADR-015
    AI-Off contract: no AI surface leaks when the feature flag is off; view.opened telemetry deferred
    until the gate is open, mirroring the absent `data-ai-feature` marker in off mode).
Charts/maps: none in the web source → none added.
States rendered (every one, never a blank box): gated, loading (skeleton chrome), error (retryable
  gate-error / QueryError peer), ready · {idle friendly hint | no-vehicle hint | thinking indicator |
  streamed prose | inline "Helix error: …"}; plus the orthogonal P4 connectivity axis live/stale/offline
  (freshness chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition; offline never auto-refreshes).
i18n keys (web source keys verbatim, resolved through P1/S10 — no English literals in code):
